    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_methodological_critique_validity",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "The measure is reliable in the sense that it is consistent, but its validity is questionable because it may not capture the construct we care about."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "سنجش از نظر ثبات پایاست، ولی اعتبارش محل سؤاله چون شاید اصلاً سازه‌ای رو که برامون مهمه اندازه نگیره."
        },
        "intent": "separate_validity_reliability",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_methodological_critique_validity",
          "c2_methodological_critique_reliability"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "school-study",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_methodological_critique_selection",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-01",
        "text": {
          "en": "Selection bias is a serious concern because participation was voluntary and the most dissatisfied users were more likely to respond."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "سوگیری انتخاب نگرانی جدیه چون شرکت داوطلبانه بوده و ناراضی‌ترین کاربران احتمال بیشتری برای پاسخ دادن داشتن."
        },
        "intent": "identify_selection_bias",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_methodological_critique_selection_bias",
          "c2_methodological_critique_generalizability"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "school-study",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_methodological_critique_measurement",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "The apparent improvement could partly reflect a change in measurement rather than a change in the underlying behavior."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "بهبود ظاهری ممکنه بخشی از تغییر در روش سنجش باشه نه تغییر در رفتار واقعی."
        },
        "intent": "question_measurement",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_methodological_critique_measurement",
          "c2_methodological_critique_validity"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "school-study",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_methodological_critique_confounder",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-02",
        "text": {
          "en": "Without a strategy for the obvious confounders, the causal interpretation remains substantially weaker than the descriptive finding."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "بدون راهی برای کنترل عوامل مداخله‌گر واضح، تفسیر علّی خیلی ضعیف‌تر از یافته توصیفی باقی می‌مونه."
        },
        "intent": "limit_causal_inference",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_methodological_critique_confounder",
          "c2_methodological_critique_causal"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "school-study",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_methodological_critique_replication",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "A failed replication does not automatically invalidate the original study; it may reveal a boundary condition or hidden dependency."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "تکرار ناموفق لزوماً مطالعه اصلی رو باطل نمی‌کنه؛ ممکنه یک شرط مرزی یا وابستگی پنهان رو آشکار کنه."
        },
        "intent": "interpret_replication",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_methodological_critique_replication",
          "c2_methodological_critique_validity"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "school-study",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_methodological_critique_general",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "The sample supports inference about this population reasonably well, but generalizability beyond it is speculative."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "نمونه برای استنتاج درباره همین جمعیت نسبتاً خوبه، ولی تعمیم فراتر از اون حدسیه."
        },
        "intent": "scope_generalizability",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_methodological_critique_generalizability",
          "c2_methodological_critique_selection_bias"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "school-study",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_methodological_critique_causal",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "The design establishes temporal order, which is necessary for a causal claim but nowhere near sufficient on its own."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "طراحی ترتیب زمانی رو مشخص می‌کنه که برای ادعای علّی لازمه، ولی به‌تنهایی اصلاً کافی نیست."
        },
        "intent": "calibrate_causal_claim",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_methodological_critique_causal",
          "c2_methodological_critique_confounder"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "school-study",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "utterance",
      "external_id": "u_c2_methodological_critique_summary",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-03",
        "text": {
          "en": "Methodological critique should identify what the design supports, what it cannot establish and which limitation matters most for the conclusion."
        },
        "translations": {
          "fa": "نقد روش‌شناسی باید مشخص کنه طراحی چی رو پشتیبانی می‌کنه، چی رو نمی‌تونه ثابت کنه و کدوم محدودیت برای نتیجه مهم‌تره."
        },
        "intent": "summarize_method_critique",
        "concept_refs": [
          "c2_methodological_critique_validity",
          "c2_methodological_critique_generalizability",
          "c2_methodological_critique_measurement"
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "school-study",
        "register": "neutral",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_methodological_critique_advanced_hedging",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-01",
        "slug": "c2-methodological-critique-advanced-hedging",
        "title": "Advanced hedging and calibration",
        "rule_summary": "Calibrate certainty with expressions such as arguably, broadly speaking, tends to, appears to, and cannot entirely be ruled out.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در C1 میزان قطعیت را با عبارت‌هایی مثل arguably، broadly speaking، tends to، appears to و cannot entirely be ruled out دقیق تنظیم می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The change appears to have improved access, although the evidence is still limited.",
            "fa": "به نظر می‌رسد این تغییر دسترسی را بهتر کرده، هرچند شواهد هنوز محدود است."
          },
          {
            "en": "That explanation cannot entirely be ruled out.",
            "fa": "نمی‌توان آن توضیح را کاملاً منتفی دانست."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_methodological_critique_nominalisation",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-02",
        "slug": "c2-methodological-critique-nominalisation",
        "title": "Nominalisation in formal discourse",
        "rule_summary": "Turn verbs or adjectives into noun phrases to make formal arguments more compact and abstract when appropriate.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "در گفتار و نوشتار رسمی، در صورت مناسب بودن فعل یا صفت را به عبارت اسمی تبدیل می‌کنیم تا استدلال فشرده‌تر و انتزاعی‌تر شود."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The rapid expansion of the service created new risks.",
            "fa": "گسترش سریع سرویس ریسک‌های جدیدی ایجاد کرد."
          },
          {
            "en": "A reduction in waiting times would benefit everyone.",
            "fa": "کاهش زمان انتظار به نفع همه خواهد بود."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "grammar_point",
      "external_id": "g_c2_methodological_critique_reporting_passive",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-03",
        "slug": "c2-methodological-critique-reporting-passive",
        "title": "Impersonal reporting structures",
        "rule_summary": "Use structures such as is thought to, is believed to, and has been reported to when the source is general or deliberately backgrounded.",
        "explanation": {
          "fa": "وقتی منبع عمومی است یا عمداً در پس‌زمینه قرار می‌گیرد از ساختارهایی مثل is thought to، is believed to و has been reported to استفاده می‌کنیم."
        },
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "The policy is thought to have reduced short-term demand.",
            "fa": "گمان می‌رود این سیاست تقاضای کوتاه‌مدت را کاهش داده باشد."
          },
          {
            "en": "The company is reported to be reconsidering the plan.",
            "fa": "گزارش شده شرکت در حال بازنگری برنامه است."
          }
        ],
        "cefr": "C2",
        "status": "approved"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "dialogue",
      "external_id": "d_c2_methodological_critique_scene_1",
      "data": {
        "lesson_key": "c2-methodological-critique-01",
        "title": "Methodological Critique & Epistemic Limits: part 1",
        "setting": "professional workshop",
        "cefr": "C2",
        "topic": "school-study",
        "characters": [
          "Ivy",
          "David"
        ],
        "turns": [
          {
            "order": 1,
            "speaker": "Ivy",
            "text": "How would you respond without making the disagreement personal?",
            "translation_fa": "چطور جواب می‌دادی بدون اینکه مخالفت شخصی بشه؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 2,
            "speaker": "David",
            "text": "The measure is reliable in the sense that it is consistent, but its validity is questionable because it may not capture the construct we care about.",
            "translation_fa": "سنجش از نظر ثبات پایاست، ولی اعتبارش محل سؤاله چون شاید اصلاً سازه‌ای رو که برامون مهمه اندازه نگیره."
          },
          {
            "order": 3,
            "speaker": "Ivy",
            "text": "What could you concede while still holding your position?",
            "translation_fa": "چی رو می‌تونی بپذیری و در عین حال موضعت رو حفظ کنی؟"
          },
          {
            "order": 4,
            "speaker": "David",
            "text": "Selection bias is a serious concern because participation was voluntary and the most dissatisfied users were more likely to respond.",
            "translation_fa": "سوگیری انتخاب نگرانی جدیه چون شرکت داوطلبانه بوده و ناراضی‌ترین کاربران احتمال بیشتری برای پاسخ دادن داشتن."
          }
        ],
